{"name":"Azure Green Blue","hex":"#006c81","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"azure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The clear blue colour of the sky; also, a pigment or dye of this colour.","A blue colour on a coat of arms, represented in engraving by horizontal parallel lines."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sky blue; resembling the clear blue colour of the unclouded sky.","Cloudless."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/azure"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Azure (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Azure is the color between cyan and blue on the color wheel. It is often described as the color of the sky on a clear day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Azulejos_Parque_Eduardo_VII-2.jpg/330px-Azulejos_Parque_Eduardo_VII-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azure_(color)","wikidata":"Q373058"},{"title":"Blue-green","blocks":[{"text":"Blue-green is the color between blue and green. It belongs to the cyan family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Color_star-en.svg/330px-Color_star-en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue-green","wikidata":"Q646964"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/ChalcanthitefranceII.jpg/500px-ChalcanthitefranceII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/ChalcanthitefranceII.jpg/1280px-ChalcanthitefranceII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/ChalcanthitefranceII.jpg/500px-ChalcanthitefranceII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChalcanthitefranceII.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_%28cropped%29_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_%28cropped%29_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_%28cropped%29_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_%28cropped%29_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_%28cropped%29_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_%28cropped%29_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlcedo_azurea_-_Julatten_(cropped)_2_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/TfNSW_T4_%28cropped_2%29.png/120px-TfNSW_T4_%28cropped_2%